    "facts_line": "2026-10-30 (Friday, before the open), 7 days out -- from the earnings calendar, consensus EPS 2.62.",
    "why": "The trading update already flagged refining margins at $46.7/bbl and net debt near $14bn; the print must turn both into cash."
  },
  "reasons": [
    "The 13 October trading statement pre-announced the quarter: refining margins at $46.7/bbl, triple last year, and net debt guided to $13.5-14.5bn from $22.3bn in Q2 -- none of it is in the June figures.",
    "Cutting net debt by roughly $8bn in one quarter reduces interest expense from the $1.18bn a quarter BP paid in June, lifting earnings with no extra barrels sold.",
    "Supply sets the price: the February Hormuz closure removed about 10 mb/d [million barrels a day] of crude, nearly four times the IEA's [International Energy Agency] 2.6 mb/d demand fall for 2026, so upstream cash holds."
  ],
  "watch": [
    "Refining margin: confirms at the $46.7/bbl flagged in the trading statement; breaks if the realised margin falls well short of it.",
    "Net debt: confirms inside the guided $13.5-14.5bn; breaks above $14.5bn, or if the cut came from disposals rather than cash.",
    "Q3 adjusted profit: confirms near Goldman's $7.49bn estimate; breaks at or below the $2.62 consensus EPS.",
    "Impairments: confirms within the flagged $3-4.5bn gas and low-carbon write-down; breaks if it runs higher."
  ],
